From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Modeling Algorithms - BRepFilletAPI_MakeFillet builds fillets whose
 arcs cross, and fillets that run out of face, after the stripe builder fails

Two fillets on opposite edges of a face with r1 + r2 > w (a 4 mm face, 3 and 3), and a single fillet
whose radius is at least the width of the face it sits on (r >= 4 on a 4 mm face), make
BRepFilletAPI_MakeFillet answer IsDone() == false. In the first case ChFi3d_Builder::PerformOneCorner
and ChFi3d_StripeEdgeInter refuse the crossing caps and contact curves; in the second the contact
line on the far face lies outside the face and the stripe has no start solution (StripeStatus
ChFiDS_StartsolFailure). Open-Cascade-SAS/OCCT#1177, both halves.

The stripe builder only knows a stripe that cuts a face; two stripes that cross need a
surface-surface section curve in the data structure, and a fillet that runs out of face needs an
edge as its second support. This change does not add that. It adds the behaviour for the cases a
box shows, after Compute() has failed, in BRepFilletAPI_MakeFillet::Build:

 - Contours that share no vertex, all of constant radius: the intersection (BRepAlgoAPI_Common) of the
   shape filleted on each contour alone. Each arc stays tangent to the face it starts on and the arcs
   cross on the face between them at an included angle below 180 degrees.
 - A single straight edge between two planar rectangles at a right angle: where a face runs out
   before the tangent point, its far edge is the pivot. The arc stays tangent to the other face and
   passes through the pivot, or passes through both far edges when both run out. The shape is cut by
   the prism of the region between the arc and the faces.

Every result must be a valid closed solid (BRepCheck_Analyzer, one solid, every edge on two faces),
must take material away, must remove no more than the sum and no less than the maximum of what each
contour removes, and for the pivot cut must remove exactly cross-section area times edge length.
Otherwise Build leaves the failure as it was. Contours that share a vertex, evolving radii, curved or
non-rectangular faces and concave edges are not covered and still fail as before.

ChFi3d_Builder gains the inline accessor InitialShape(). TKFillet lists TKPrim, which it already
links through TKBO. After a fallback result the builder is reset: faulty contours read zero, and
Modified, Generated and IsDeleted know nothing of the new faces.

Measured (Scripts/repro/fillet-pivot-edges/): on a 4 x 10 x 6 box, radii 2.2 to 3.9 equal and
unequal on the two top edges, a single fillet of 4 to 6.5, 4 x 10 x 3 with 4.5, a 10 x 10 x 3 plate,
and a fillet next to a finished fillet: valid, closed, tessellating, deterministic, volumes within
1e-11 (relative) of the analytic section, the cylinders tangent to their walls to 0 degrees and the
crease angles equal to the formulas. 715 box cases before and after: 312 valid ones identical in
volume and face count, 331 unchanged outcomes, 70 IsDone false now valid, none newly invalid.
tests/bugs/moddata_1/bug119 still fails as it must; OCCT#1177's one-side sample (a 10 cube, r = 10)
now builds.

Tracked as SecondMouseAU/OCCTSwift#3208.

---
